  "reason": "The records collectively disclose the essential processing strategy and strengthening rationale. Multiple refractory-HEA studies use mechanical or high-energy ball milling of elemental powders followed by short-duration vacuum SPS, showing solid-solution formation, densification, milling-time-dependent refinement, and hardness near 675 HV. Other records directly connect nanocrystalline grains to Hall–Petch strengthening and identify dislocation accumulation, severe plastic deformation, and solid-solution strain fields as strength sources. Thus an expert could plausibly transfer the combined HEBM–SPS approach and synergistic grain-boundary/dislocation/solid-solution mechanism to CoCrFeNiTi, although the precise 1–6 h milling window, 900–1000 °C SPS conditions, and 83% FCC/17% BCC phase balance are not specifically anticipated."
